  "details": "<p>Salvage excavation identified the site of Boncuklu Tarla in 2008. Scientific excavation began in 2012 alongside the\u00a0<span>Il\u0131su Dam project. The site represents a rare and seemingly uninterrupted\u00a0</span>archaeological sequence for the preceramic Neolithic in the Upper Tigris Valley.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Boncuklu Tarla is an archaeological site located in the Mardin province of Turkey. The human settlement was occupied from the Late Epipalaeolithic to Pre-Pottery Neolithic B periods.",
